# ip6tables rules for ZeroTier IPv6 gateway
# Map into container: -v /volume1/docker/zerotier/iptables:/etc/iptables
# File path inside container: /etc/iptables/rules.v6
#
# NOTE: This file is a reference template. install.sh writes the production
# copy to $DATA_DIR/iptables/rules.v6 with actual interface names substituted.
#
# IPv6 uses global unicast addresses — NAT is not needed or used.
# ip6tables-restore is ATOMIC: a single invalid line aborts the entire restore.

# Clamp TCP MSS to PMTU so that large-MSS segments don't black-hole when the
# ZeroTier overlay MTU (typically ~1400B effective) is less than the physical
# NIC MTU (1500B). Applies on both directions of every SYN or SYN-ACK.
*mangle
-A FORWARD -p tcp --tcp-flags SYN,RST SYN -j TCPMSS --clamp-mss-to-pmtu
COMMIT

# Allow ZeroTier-to-LAN and LAN-to-ZeroTier IPv6 forwarding.
# ICMPv6 MUST be permitted for Neighbor Discovery (NDP), PMTU discovery,
# and Router Advertisements — blocking it breaks all IPv6 connectivity.
*filter
-A FORWARD -i zt+ -o eth0 -j ACCEPT
-A FORWARD -i zt+ -o eth1 -j ACCEPT
-A FORWARD -i eth0 -o zt+ -j ACCEPT
-A FORWARD -i eth1 -o zt+ -j ACCEPT
-A FORWARD -p icmpv6 -j ACCEPT
-A FORWARD -m conntrack --ctstate RELATED,ESTABLISHED -j ACCEPT
COMMIT
